@@ -0,0 +1,70 @@
+# Todo Due Dates Implementation Plan
+
+> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [x]`) syntax for tracking.
+
+**Goal:** Implement ticket #1: optional due dates, UTC overdue status, API filtering, and a read-only list with an overdue-only control.
+
+**Architecture:** Keep the singleton `TodoStore` shared by the JSON API and Blazor circuit. Use calendar dates and a shared UTC overdue predicate; preserve missing versus explicitly null PATCH fields. The UI calls the store directly and adds no HTTP calls.
+
+**Tech Stack:** .NET 10, Blazor Interactive Server, System.Text.Json, xUnit, existing WebApplicationFactory; no new NuGet packages.
+
+**Spec:** Ticket #1, Approved Spec comment (scope agreed in this conversation; posted to the ticket).
+
+## Global Constraints
+
+- Optional JSON `dueDate`: exact `YYYY-MM-DD`, or null; `isOverdue` in every todo response.
+- Overdue means not done and due date strictly before the current UTC date. Today, future, done, and no date are never overdue.
+- POST accepts the date; PATCH omission preserves it, a date replaces it, null removes it.
+- Invalid dates return HTTP 400 with an `error` property. Store validation uses `ValidationException`.
+- `GET /todos?overdue=true` selects overdue, `false` selects non-overdue, omission selects all.
+- UI displays dates and the exact word "überfällig"; a control labeled "nur überfällige" filters the list.
+- No UI editing, sorting, reminders, styling, persistence changes, or new packages.
+- Give new test-dependent UI elements `data-testid` attributes.
+- Agent runs end-to-end browser checks with Playwright, evidence outside the repository, and shuts down the app.
+- Branch `1_faelligkeitsdatum_todos`; draft PR to main named `WIP: 1: Fälligkeitsdatum für Todos`. Never merge or close the ticket.
+
+## Review Focus
+
+- Explicit null PATCH clears a date while an unrelated PATCH preserves it (Task 1 API tests).
+- A non-UTC host timezone must not change the UTC date boundary (Task 1 fixed-time predicate tests).
+- Invalid dates, timestamps, and empty strings cannot mutate a valid todo (Task 1 API and store tests).
+- The UI filter excludes completed/no-date/today todos and can be turned off again (Task 2 browser check).
+- Updated dates and completion status are reflected after reload, including while filtered (Task 2 browser check).
+
+### Task 1: Store and API due dates, overdue status, and filtering
+
+**Files:** Modify `src/DemoTodo/TodoStore.cs`, `src/DemoTodo/Program.cs`, `tests/DemoTodo.Tests/TodoStoreTests.cs`, `tests/DemoTodo.Tests/TodoApiTests.cs`.
+
+**Interfaces:** `Todo` gains optional `DateOnly? DueDate` and computed `bool IsOverdue`; a shared `IsOverdueOn(DateOnly today)` predicate permits deterministic calendar-boundary tests. `NewTodo` accepts optional `string? DueDate`; `TodoPatch` tracks whether its `DueDate` property was supplied. `TodoStore.List(bool? overdue = null)` returns the selected todos in existing order. Parse date strings strictly and centrally in the store.
+
+- [x] Add failing store tests for optional dates, date validation, PATCH set/replace/remove/preserve, and UTC overdue cases. Predicate assertions include:
+
+```csharp
+Assert.True(new Todo(1, "A", false, new DateOnly(2026, 10, 20))
+    .IsOverdueOn(new DateOnly(2026, 10, 21)));
+Assert.False(new Todo(1, "A", false, new DateOnly(2026, 10, 21))
+    .IsOverdueOn(new DateOnly(2026, 10, 21)));
+```
+
+- [x] Run `dotnet test --filter FullyQualifiedName~TodoStoreTests`; confirm new assertions fail because the feature is missing, then implement the store/model changes and rerun.
+- [x] Update the existing exact JSON expectation to include `dueDate` and `isOverdue`. Add failing API tests proving create/read/list/patch responses, omitted/null PATCH distinction, invalid date errors and unchanged state, and all three filter modes. Example assertions: POST with `dueDate = "2026-10-20"` returns that exact string; PATCH `{title:"B"}` preserves it; PATCH `{dueDate:null}` clears it.
+- [x] Run `dotnet test --filter FullyQualifiedName~TodoApiTests`; confirm filtering fails before changing the endpoint. Bind nullable `overdue` and delegate to `store.List(overdue)`; rerun `dotnet test` and require zero failures.
+- [x] Commit store, API, and tests with `feat: add todo due dates and overdue API filter`.
+
+### Task 2: Read-only due date display and interactive list filter
+
+**Files:** Modify `src/DemoTodo/Components/Pages/Home.razor`, `tests/DemoTodo.Tests/TodoApiTests.cs`.
+
+**Interfaces:** Consume Task 1's `DueDate`, `IsOverdue`, and `TodoStore.List(bool?)`. Add checkbox `data-testid="overdue-filter"`, label "nur überfällige", date `data-testid="todo-due-date"`, and marker `data-testid="todo-overdue"` containing "überfällig". Preserve existing list/item/title test IDs. Unchecked shows all; checked passes `true` to `List`.
+
+- [x] Add a failing page test with past/open, past/done, today, future, and no-date todos; assert ISO dates, exactly one overdue marker, and the labeled checkbox. Run it and confirm missing markup causes failure.
+- [x] Implement the minimal Razor markup and checkbox binding, without CSS changes. Run `dotnet test` and require zero failures.
+- [x] Start `dotnet run --project src/DemoTodo --urls http://localhost:3000`; wait for `/health`. Seed the five cases through the API, load `/`, wait for the Blazor circuit, toggle the checkbox on and off, and assert the exact visible titles and marker text.
+- [x] Through the API change/remove dates and mark a past todo complete, reload and repeat filtering; verify the UI and API filter agree. Capture screenshots outside the repo; stop the app.
+- [x] Commit UI and page tests with `feat: show and filter overdue todos on list page`.
+
+### Completion
+
+- [x] Independent whole-branch code review, address material findings, and run final `dotnet test` plus `git diff --check`.
+- [x] Push branch and create draft PR to `main` with the Implementation Summary and ticket reference.
+- [x] Post Implementation Summary and Cost Summary to ticket #1; move from `status:in-progress` to `status:review`. Leave ticket open and PR draft.
